            <ArticleTitle>Pain sensitivity, sensory deprivation and susceptibility to satiation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1431-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results reported bear out the hypotheses that (i) pain tolerance is positively related to satiability; (ii) sensory deprivation tolerance is negatively related to satiability. It is inferred that satiability may prove to be in part the mechanism of tolerance and intolerance, and that pain tolerance is inversely related to sensory deprivation tolerance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
